# Purchase Order design pattern (all pages)

## Standard look
- **Top bar**: White background, bottom border `#dee2e6`. Title as `<h1>` (24px, weight 400). Actions on the right.
- **Primary button**: Green `#28a745`, no gradient.
- **Secondary / link**: Transparent with border `#dee2e6`, or blue link `#007bff`.
- **Sections**: Neutral; bottom border only, no gradient or purple.
- **Inputs**: Underline-only (border-bottom `#dee2e6`), transparent background; focus `#80bdff`.
- **Tables**: thead `#f8f9fa`, th text `#495057`; tbody row border `#dee2e6`, hover `#f8f9fa`; total row `#f8f9fa`.
- **Modals**: thead same light gray, no purple gradient.
- **No**: `#667eea`, `#764ba2`, or gradient backgrounds for headers/cards.

## How to apply

### Option A – Global pattern (style.css)
Wrap the whole block content in:
```html
<div class="page-po">
  <div class="page-po__topbar">
    <h1 class="page-po__title">Page Title</h1>
    <div class="page-po__actions">...</div>
  </div>
  <div class="page-po__section">...</div>
  ...
</div>
```
Remove page-specific `<style>` that use gradients, `.page-header` purple, or `.card` gradient. The global `.page-po` rules in `static/css/style.css` provide the look.

Use when possible: `page-po__btn-primary`, `page-po__btn-secondary`, `page-po__link`, `page-po__section-title`, `page-po__filters`.

### Option B – Page-specific scoped classes
For complex pages (e.g. Sales, Cash Receipt New), keep a scoped wrapper (e.g. `.si-page`, `.crn-container`) and define only overrides in the template so tables, modals, and buttons match the PO look (same colors as above).

